    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Difference of squares is especially useful when a sum or difference is already known.\n\nx²−y² = (x+y)(x−y).",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If x²−y²=160 and x+y=20, then:\n20(x−y)=160\nx−y=8\n\nThe numbers would be 14 and 6 if needed. Often the question asks only for the difference.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
