    "teach_7": {
      "id": "teach_7",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A single number and its reciprocal often lead to a quadratic.\n\nSuppose x + 1/x = 5/2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_7_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_7_step": {
      "id": "teach_7_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Multiply by x:\nx² + 1 = 5x/2\n2x² − 5x + 2 = 0\n(2x−1)(x−2)=0\n\nSo x=1/2 or x=2. Reciprocal pairs naturally appear together.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_7"
        }
      ]
    },
